  <h2>Regulatory basis</h2>
  <p>This legal notice is provided pursuant to the Finnish Act on Electronic Communications Services (917/2014), the EU e-Commerce Directive (2000/31/EC), German teleservices legislation (DDG), and French requirements under the Loi pour la Confiance dans l'Économie Numérique (LCEN 2004-575).</p>

  <h2>What the service is</h2>
  <p>einvoiceops keeps track of the e-invoicing rules in {listed}, each country on its own. For each country it reads a fixed list of sources every week. When it finds a change, it tells the people who look after the parts of a customer's invoicing the change affects what changed for them and where it was published, and it keeps a record of what it sent and to whom.</p>
  <p>The service helps a company prepare for changes to e-invoicing rules. What it sends is a reading of a change with its source beside it, so the reader can check it.</p>

  <h2>What the service is not</h2>
  <p>einvoiceops is not a law firm, licensed legal advisor, certified tax consultant, or compliance authority. No content on this site, and nothing sent through the paid service, constitutes legal advice, tax advice, or a compliance opinion.</p>
  <p>Preparing for a change is not the same as compliance assurance. Whether a company's preparation makes it compliant in its own circumstances is a determination that requires qualified legal and tax counsel with full knowledge of that company's entity structure, VAT registrations, contracts, and systems. einvoiceops does not make that determination and does not represent that its outputs do. In particular, it does not:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>give a legal interpretation of how a rule applies to a particular company,</li>
    <li>give tax advice or VAT opinions,</li>
    <li>certify or sign off compliance, or confirm that a company is compliant,</li>
    <li>advise on penalty exposure or enforcement risk,</li>
    <li>resolve conflicting sources or legislative ambiguity.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>einvoiceops reports the changes it finds in the sources it reads. It does not claim to find every change to a country's rules, and what to do about a change, and when, stays with the customer.</p>

  <h2>Figures on this site</h2>
  <p>The counts on this site are the changes einvoiceops has found in the sources it reads, counted since 1 January 2024 and updated after its weekly read. They are not a count of every change made to a country's rules.</p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>Content on this site is provided for operational preparation purposes only. einvoiceops (Nomos Digital Oy) accepts no liability for decisions taken based on this content without independent legal and tax validation. Customers remain responsible for all compliance decisions, their implementation, and their legal consequences.</p>
  <p>E-invoicing rules are subject to ongoing legislative change. einvoiceops makes reasonable efforts to track and reflect those changes but does not warrant that content is current, complete, or free of error at the time of reading. Users who require current and authoritative information for compliance decisions should consult the relevant national tax authority publications and qualified legal counsel.</p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by Finnish law. Disputes are subject to the jurisdiction of Finnish courts, specifically the District Court of Espoo (Espoon käräjäoikeus) as the court of first instance, unless mandatory EU consumer protection rules require otherwise.</p>
